| shape | 1×1 | 1×2 | 1×3 | 1×4 | 2×2 | 1×5 | 2×3 | 2×4 | 3×3 | 2×5 | 3×4 | 3×5 | 4×4 | 4×5 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| area | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 8 | 9 | 10 | 12 | 15 | 16 | 20 |

(5×5 is excluded since one rectangle would be the whole grid.) Note **only area 4 has two distinct shapes** (1×4 and 2×2); every other area has at most one shape. So in any valid partition, the five chosen areas form a 5-element multiset drawn from {1,2,3,4,4,5,6,8,9,10,12,15,16,20} (4 usable at most twice, all others at most once), summing to 25.

